family: M0
corpus: C4
modes: archive bare bare-user-shared
tier: T0
outcome: unobserved
severity: interop
identity: unobserved
oracle: checksum-agreement manifest
evidence: -
spec: format-reference.md#extended-attributes
question: Confirm the stored xattr set is byte-wise name-sorted in each mode, and
 that the 1024-byte value survives. In bare mode the set lives on the object inode
 rather than in a header.
note: one value of this corpus parts the two implementations, observed in archive,
 bare, and bare-user while Phase 17c built its `commit --no-xattrs` cells: an
 xattr whose value is zero bytes long is recorded by the port and dropped by the
 tool, on a regular file and on a directory alike, so the object checksums differ
 for any tree carrying one. The loss is at ingest only -- the tool's checkout
 writes such an xattr back out of an object that carries one -- and bare-user-only
 is unaffected, discarding every xattr. Deciding what the port records is its own
 change, outside the phase that found it; until then no cell here states this
 corpus in these modes.

